# @@TITLE@@ usage

Run `@@TOOL_NAME@@` by command name through NusaLLM `exec` or `exec_session`.
The generated wrapper is placed in the selected tools directory.

Provide one JSON value either as the optional positional argument or on stdin.
When the argument is omitted, the executable reads stdin. Successful output is
one JSON value on stdout. Diagnostics go to stderr. Exit codes are 0 for success,
2 for invalid JSON input or invalid arguments, and 1 for an unhandled runtime
failure.

The implementation is `@@TOOL_NAME@@.tool/main.py`. Add tool-owned files under
`@@TOOL_NAME@@.tool/resources/`; `RESOURCE_DIR` in `main.py` resolves that path
from the implementation file, independent of the caller's working directory.
